WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.467
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.201
is a world wrestling

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.603
entertainment superstar

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.471
and 16-time world champion.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.907
He's also a talented actor
you know from "Trainwreck,"

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.509
"Blockers," and the
"Fast &amp; Furious" franchise.

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:12.311
He stars in "Peacemaker,"

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.714
which is streaming
on HBO Max January 13th.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:15.515
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.816
-♪ I could've cried ♪

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.818
♪ I could've cried ♪

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.620
♪♪

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.388
♪ When she said ♪

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:26.092
♪ I don't love you anymore ♪

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.061
Hey, I got to thank you
for tonight.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.363
-Please welcome back to the
show our friend John Cena.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.830
How are you, John?

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.232
-The beliked Seth Meyers.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.533
Beloved, in my book.

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.602
I'm very well.
How are you, sir?

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.037
-I'm very well.
Thanks for the upgrade.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.940
I think that the difference
between that clip

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.642
and the last clip we showed
when you came on

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:46.112
is maybe the most massive
switch of clips.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.947
Last time, you were jumping
through windows

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.517
and, now, we have you dancing
in your tighty-whities.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.351
Beautifully done.
Is that choreographed,

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:53.953
or is that all John Cena?

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.222
-That's interpretive dance.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.057
-I didn't think anybody was
rolling on that

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:01.827
and, now, it's for the world
to see on HBO Max

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:05.264
this Thursday, yeah.
So that's out there.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:08.000
It's a brave show.
-It's very authentic,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.136
very personal, very beautiful.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:14.239
-It's a whole lot.
It's a whole lot of Peace.

00:01:14.239 --> 00:01:15.874
No, I mean, you know,

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:19.612
depending on what you see,
depending on what you see.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.181
-Now, you're wearing
the costume, John,

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:25.818
but we do not see the helmet,
the iconic helmet,

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:28.555
because you lost it
last evening.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.323
-That son of a bitch Fallon.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.057
-Yep.
-I lost it in a sucker's bet.

00:01:32.057 --> 00:01:33.526
We play games all the time

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.928
and I always win
and there's no stakes,

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.832
so I go in pretty much
undefeated

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.333
and I bet that he had
to frost his tips

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.067
and I bet him
the Peacemaker helmet

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.171
and, yeah,
I lost the Peacemaker helmet,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.406
that I don't own,
to Jimmy Fallon in a sucker bet.

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:49.042
That son of a bitch.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.810
-I mean, you think the stakes
were high for you.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.978
Here I am, watching it last
night, thinking, "I can't wait.

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.981
I get to have the helmet guy
on my show."

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.917
Nothing.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.253
-Yeah, and, now, you just got
a guy with blue gloves, yeah.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.921
Such a letdown.
So sorry.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.757
-This is so fun.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.960
Peacemaker was such a fun
character to play for you,

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.362
for me to watch,
in "Suicide Squad"

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:14.500
and, now, right after, we get
to see it in its own show.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.103
A different kind of superhero,
sort of damaged,

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:20.272
sort of raunchy,
sort of crass and arrogant

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:22.775
and all things that, I think,
if we actually had superheroes,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.543
we would probably see a lot more

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:28.314
than maybe the superheroes
we've been fed over the years.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.083
-So, hero is virtue.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:32.718
Superhero is super virtue.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:36.589
Peacemaker is a guy
who kills for peace

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.624
and he's really good
at what he does

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.661
and he's really, really flawed.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.129
And I think that's
when you say like,

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.098
"If we could see all those
things in superheroes,

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.699
it would probably be
more authentic."

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.067
That's because we're all human.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.735
Superheroes are
all super virtuous.

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:52.104
Peacemaker is jealous
of all these superheroes.

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.406
There was an Aquaman clip
that went viral,

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:55.941
that Peacemaker released,

00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:58.845
Peacemaker's thoughts
on Aquaman,

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.680
and it just goes to show
that he's like,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.381
jealous of real superheroes.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.884
And I think that makes
for an awesome, funny journey.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.620
We have a wonderful cast
to surround Peacemaker

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.722
and it kind of explores the fact
that this guy,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.658
with this set of skills,
thinks he's a superhero,

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:16.628
but his perspective on life
may be a little bit upside-down.

00:03:16.628 --> 00:03:17.730
-Is there something --

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.265
It must feel similar, at times,

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:22.602
the performative nature of what
you're doing with Peacemaker,

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.937
compared to your, you know,

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:26.272
long and illustrious career
in WWE.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:31.143
I mean, there is a cinematic
universe to the WWE.

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:32.978
There is the building
of heroes and villains.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:34.413
I mean, did you feel
that parallel

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.516
when you entered
the superhero world?

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.184
-Kind of,
but it was the opposite.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:42.888
So, in WWE, the John Cena
character is one of virtue,

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:45.558
one of hard work,
loyalty, respect,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.059
never giving up, persistence,

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.529
always, even when your back
is against the wall,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.797
trying to do
the morally right thing.

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:52.898
So this one was easy.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:53.732
I would just have to say like,

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:55.200
"Okay, what I do in WWE?"

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.003
Do the opposite of that
and add some profanity

00:03:58.003 --> 00:04:01.507
and that's Peacemaker.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.877
-You know, obviously, now,
we've come to

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:08.514
not be surprised by the
comedic chops you've shown

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.283
in things like "Trainwreck"
and things like "Blockers."

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:14.019
Were you happy when you first
got that chance to do it?

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:17.490
Were you pleased with how easy
it came to you?

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:21.627
-So, man, thank you very much
for the flattery.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:24.330
You have to remember,
in those films,

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.332
in any forum I do comedy in,

00:04:27.332 --> 00:04:30.369
I want to be able to surround
myself with really funny people

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:34.306
and funny people know how
to draw the funny out of others,

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.843
even if it's at their expense,
which I also don't mind,

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.411
which makes me
a nice target for comedy.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.480
But I think,
in all those circumstances,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.981
especially starting
with "Trainwreck,"

00:04:42.981 --> 00:04:47.453
you know, Judd casts amazingly
and Amy was so giving

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.921
and provided
such a great environment.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.557
I think it's just, for me,

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.526
it's been great to surround
myself with funny people

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.327
and allow them to just tee off

00:04:55.327 --> 00:05:00.033
and then just kind of be present
to see what's going on.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:02.702
-One of your costars is one
of our favorite on this show,

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.003
Danielle Brooks.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.738
-Oh, dude, that's great.
-I need to ask --

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.208
have you seen Danielle
make balloon animals yet?

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:12.145
-I haven't.
What is that process all about?

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.680
-I would just say ask Danielle
to make you a balloon animal

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.015
and just know
that you haven't lived yet.

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:18.584
You haven't lived yet.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.818
-Ah!

00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:21.754
With someone with an incredible
lust for life,

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.189
I can't wait to see
these balloon animals.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:26.492
-I learned --
I heard, I should say --

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:31.063
that you had to learn
some sword skills for the show.

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:34.199
Did you take to the sword?

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.902
-It took a while
to take to the sword.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:39.138
You see a lot of sword
in the "Suicide Squad."

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:42.574
You pretty much see me dancing
with my sword in "Peacemaker."

00:05:42.574 --> 00:05:44.209
-[ Laughs ]
-There's a lot of weaponry.

00:05:44.209 --> 00:05:47.012
There's a lot of weaponry mixed
with vulgarity in "Peacemaker"

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:51.551
and you'll probably see my sword
more than a sword.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:54.286
I think we have a chain saw
in there, somewhere.

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:55.788
Yeah, there's a lot of stuff.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.456
There's a lot of stuff.

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.024
-A lot of sharp edges.

00:05:59.024 --> 00:06:01.294
Now, this is something
that I was surprised to hear,

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.329
but maybe shame on me
for being surprised.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:06.866
You're a man who contains
multitudes.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:09.368
-[ Laughs ]
-Is it true that you are also,

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:14.340
John Cena is a man who's happy
to walk into an antique shop?

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.941
-Oh, yeah, I love antiques.

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:19.512
Like, man, I really do.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.013
I love going antiquing.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:23.682
I love trying to find out the
story behind all these objects.

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:26.284
I don't necessarily --

00:06:26.284 --> 00:06:28.687
Although I love finding value
and look for bargains,

00:06:28.687 --> 00:06:30.389
it's more the story
and the object

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:32.958
that I find really exciting.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:36.595
And I just, I don't know,
there's something about

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:39.799
an object with pedigree,
an object with a story.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.267
I don't know.
Maybe it's the imagination,

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:44.270
but, yes, I do absolutely
love antiquing.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.404
You can tell that this
struck a nerve.

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:47.006
I got the spirit fingers.

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.507
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:49.842
Antiquing! Ooh!

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:51.911
-I've never seen you
like this, John.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.346
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:55.681
Now, I'm not surprised
to hear that,

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.316
in your younger days,
you were a bouncer.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.652
I think anyone would be able
to track that

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:03.389
as maybe a good first job
for a young John Cena.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:05.525
But will you please tell

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:07.893
the story about being next
to a pizza shop

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:10.263
and a terrible mistake
they made,

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:12.765
not known John Cena
was working next door.

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.634
-So I was also,
like Swayze in "Roadhouse,"

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:17.336
I was the bouncer
that didn't drink.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.605
-Okay.
-It's much more
of a cooler will, yeah.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.208
I was more Sam Elliott
than Swayze, though.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:25.111
The pizza pizza place offered

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.312
free pizza,
if you could eat a full pizza,

00:07:27.312 --> 00:07:29.448
and it was Chicago
deep dish-style.

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:33.452
But I was broke and sober
at 2:00 am

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:36.321
and I literally just kept
eating pizza and eating pizza

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:37.590
and it was like
an achievement for them

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.424
and they would put
a pizza dish on the wall

00:07:39.424 --> 00:07:40.726
with your name on it.

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.995
And, by the time I had
multiple pans on the wall,

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.263
the guy realized he was getting
killed on product

00:07:45.263 --> 00:07:47.299
and on process
because he's losing a pizza pan

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:48.467
every time I eat one.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.069
-Finally, he was just like,
"Dude,

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.537
you don't have to eat the pie.

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:54.140
Come over after work for a few
slices and we got you."

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:58.143
That place was Zeppe's pizza,
that eventually closed.

00:07:58.143 --> 00:07:59.545
I'm not saying I had anything
to do with it,

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:00.879
but I probably didn't help
their bottom line

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:02.781
or their profit-loss statement.

00:08:02.781 --> 00:08:04.816
-That's true. But, at least,
I think they would --

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:07.252
In the way that antiques
have a great story,

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:10.456
at least, they have one to share
about a young John Cena

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.391
putting them out of business.
-Somewhere, there's two or three

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.026
Zeppe's pizza trays

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:17.863
with "John Cena," the date,
my weight, and "I did it."

00:08:17.863 --> 00:08:19.197
Yeah, so those
are floating around.

00:08:19.197 --> 00:08:22.334
Maybe, one of these days,
at one of these flea markets.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.570
-Thanks for being here.
You know what I'm going

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.439
to actually look for
at an antique shop

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.773
is that helmet
you lost to Fallon

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.275
because you know Fallon
sold it, first thing.

00:08:30.275 --> 00:08:31.310
-Dude, he couldn't --

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.811
He thought I took it with him

00:08:32.811 --> 00:08:33.746
when I left the show

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.080
and I totally gave it to him

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.416
and he wanted to use it
as a prop for his next skit

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.718
and he's like, "If Cena took it,
I'm going to be so pissed,"

00:08:39.718 --> 00:08:41.253
and the lady's like,
"No, here it is.

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:42.621
It's really yours."

00:08:42.621 --> 00:08:45.191
-Yeah, I would've loved
to have seen what happened

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:47.859
when Jimmy Fallon was so pissed
with John Cena.

00:08:47.859 --> 00:08:49.828
[ Laughs ]
-I would've loved to have seen
how that turned out.

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:53.499
[ Laughing ]
-Wow, man, yeah.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:55.201
-Hey, congrats on the show.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.303
I've watched the first one.
It's so much fun.

00:08:57.303 --> 00:09:00.239
You were so right
about how great the cast is

00:09:00.239 --> 00:09:01.173
and I can't wait to see more.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.874
Thanks for being here, John.

00:09:02.874 --> 00:09:04.543
-As always, thank you.

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:05.711
-John Cena, everybody.

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:08.881
"Peacemaker" is streaming
on HBO Max January 13th.

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:09.682
We'll be right back.

